;;; M1a S1a.6.6 — a NESTED FACT in a goal binding.
;;;
;;; The sibling of `int-goal-binding.ein`, found the same way and in the same
;;; family: `goal_bindings` returns the *stored* argument, and a nested
;;; argument is stored as a `Fact`. `json.dumps` cannot serialise one, so
;;;
;;;     ein.py   raised TypeError, wrote NO summary, exited 1
;;;     ein.rs   rendered `(u0 o1)` and exited 0
;;;
;;; Here ein.py — the oracle — was the one that was wrong: a crash is not a
;;; semantics anyone wants to preserve (Q-M1a.4's words for the same choice).
;;; `cli/_summary.py::_binding_value` now renders a non-primitive binding the
;;; way every other fact in that file is rendered, which is what ein.rs
;;; already did.
;;;
;;; Fixed 2026-08-20 in ein.py. This file is the regression.

(u0 o1)
(r1 (u0 o1) o2)

(query :goal (r1 ?x ?y))
